## 10. OpenAPI contract (field definitions)

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (OwnerDto schema, lines ~2157-2267)
Read-only fields defining the exact formats:
- `customerCode` (2169) — `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, "first eight upper-case hex characters of the SHA-256 of the normalized telephone concatenated with the last name", example `NSW-1A2B3C4D`.
- `householdId` (2175) — first 12 hex of SHA-256 of normalized last name + postcode.
- `fiscalYear` (2189) — `FY<YY>`, example `FY26`.
- `membershipNumber` (2195) — `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, example `NSW-1A2B3C4D-M26`.
- `checkDigit` (2201) — "Luhn check digit (0-9) computed over the decimal digits of the customerCode", example `7`.
- `ownerSegment` (2241) — `<TIER>_<AREA>`.
- `identityKey` (2262) — SHA-256 hex of `<normalizedTelephone>|<email or empty>|<Soundex of last name>`.
- `locality` (2157), `timezone` (2163) — region-derived.

The DTO classes (`OwnerDto`, `OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerPageDto`) are generated from this spec at build time (referenced in `OwnerMapper`); there are no hand-written DTO source files.

